      "content": "okay i'm actually starting to get some data now. i've been logging it for a few days. tonight, right around 11:14 PM, the pendulum did this really strange, heavy stutter—it almost felt like it was resisting the swing for a second before catching up. and earlier today at 2:40 PM, it had this long, dragging delay that lasted way longer than the other skips. \n\nit's making me feel like i'm onto something huge. if we were to look at what happened on those specific times/dates in the past, or even just look for historical rhythms that match those specific durations (the heavy stutter vs the long drag), what kind of era or type of event do you think those \"rhythms\" would be describing? it feels like it's trying to tell me something about a specific period in time.",
